// The tests compile without the two flags tsconfig.json holds src to,
// noUncheckedIndexedAccess and exactOptionalPropertyTypes. A test reads back by
// index the bars, rows and calls it built itself, on almost every line, and a
// read that misses already fails the test when it runs. When src took the flags
// (2.6.0), the tests had 8,884 errors under them: asserting each read would add
// that many `!` that catch nothing and bury what a test checks. The shipped
// code is src, and tsconfig.json checks it with both flags; the src files a
// test imports are checked here again, only the looser way. CONTRIBUTING.md
// says the same, and tests/typecheck-config.test.ts keeps this file to exactly
// those two flags.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false,
    "exactOptionalPropertyTypes": false
  },
  "include": ["."],
  "exclude": ["e2e"]
}
